## One judgment call worth flagging, not blocking

The spec's threshold logic (secondary axis when the KV ceiling is >10% off the total-in-system max)
was verified on real data only for the "far" case -- every real run in the available data set had a
ceiling several times the in-system max (ratios of ~2.9x and ~10x on two different runs), none
landed near the 10% boundary naturally. Verified the "near" (primary-axis) code path via one
synthetically-adjusted bundle (capacity value edited to land ~5% off), documented as such in both the
status file and the review trigger rather than presented as a real-data confirmation. If a future run
lands genuinely near the boundary, worth a spot-check that the real behavior matches this synthetic
test.

